WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.240
Gojo is so insanely powerful, that even Gege&nbsp;
Akutami, the author of Jujutsu Kaisen himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.880
had no other chose but to temporarily&nbsp;
completely remove him from the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:15.840
during the Shibuya incident, for&nbsp;
there to be any stakes or conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:21.240
left in the story that Gojo wouldn’t just&nbsp;
solve immediately by himself. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:27.240
there’s one thing he has that really held him back&nbsp;
in the latest episode of Jujutsu Kaisen: Trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:33.760
not to be a mass murderer. Or if you want to&nbsp;
phrase it a bit more nicely: his conscience.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.880
He DOES accept that he can’t save every&nbsp;
single person while a monstrous curse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:44.080
is wreaking havoc. However, he’ll still&nbsp;
always stop short of killing any innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:50.440
bystanders himself. His enemies know this and&nbsp;
that’s why they created the perfect plan to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.760
seal Gojo away in the Prism Realm during&nbsp;
the Shibuya Incident. Happy Halloween.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.680
Having Gojo sealed in the Prism Realm changed&nbsp;
the entire world of Jujutsu Kaisen. As many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.200
characters have hinted, Satoru Gojo’s&nbsp;
power as a Jujutsu Sorcerer is pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:13.040
much the only thing preventing curses from&nbsp;
overrunning Japan. This era’s sorcerers are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:18.960
supposedly far weaker than those of the&nbsp;
past and without Gojo’s amazing Limitless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.680
and Six-Eyes powers keeping the curses at&nbsp;
bay, the entire world is at risk - which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:32.720
exactly why it’s so bad that the plan to&nbsp;
seal Gojo worked. But what if it didn’t?

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.440
As you’ll remember, Gojo could have destroyed&nbsp;
all of his attackers in no time at all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.400
but his attack also would have caught the&nbsp;
hundreds, if not thousands of innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:49.880
civilians trapped in shibuya with him as well.&nbsp;
But what if instead, Satoru Gojo said screw it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:57.560
and got to display his full power? If just this&nbsp;
once, Gojo decided to pass on his Batman “No-Kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:04.360
Rule”, how would he fare against the combined&nbsp;
efforts of Jogo, Dagon, Hanami, Choso, Mahito,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:09.520
AND his old best friend Geto, who actually&nbsp;
isn’t really Geto, but you get what I mean??

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:14.760
There are a few reasons Gojo might decide to&nbsp;
not hold back and go all out here: First off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:20.440
maybe his Geto senses go off and he realizes that&nbsp;
if he doesn’t put an end to his old pal right then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:27.280
and there, there’ll be a lot of casualties.&nbsp;
Maybe all the train tracks remind him of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:34.360
trolley problem and he does the math and realizes&nbsp;
he’ll save way more people if he sacrifices all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:38.880
of the train station people. Maybe he just wants&nbsp;
to get into the Halloween Spirit by committing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:45.440
mass murder - the reason doesn’t matter: what&nbsp;
matters is how much he’s gonna crush these curses.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:51.760
So let’s start with the first combatants:&nbsp;
The disaster curses. This is the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.920
time Gojo’s had to deal with Jogo&nbsp;
and the third time he’s dealt with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.920
Hanami. He has no more patience at&nbsp;
all for these special grade curses.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:04.520
In the actual story, he toys&nbsp;
with them as he always does,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:11.680
but not this time. He’s going to absolutely&nbsp;
destroy these guys. Due to their teamwork,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.320
Hanami is able to cancel out Gojo’s cursed&nbsp;
technique, making Jogo the first curse in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:22.320
a while who’s actually able to touch the&nbsp;
world’s strongest sorcerer. Big mistake.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.600
Jogo’s power is fire and lava, which burns&nbsp;
bright red. You know what else is red? Gojo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:33.840
Cursed Technique Reversal: Red. This&nbsp;
insanely strong Jujutsu power passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:39.280
down through the Gojo has the ability&nbsp;
to repel things using a huge shockwave.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:44.720
Jogo has grasped onto Gojo’s arm (Note to the&nbsp;
author Gege Akutami - thank you for making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:51.960
these characters’ names so similar).&nbsp;
Jogo’s grip slightly burns his sleeve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:56.680
but his single eye barely has time&nbsp;
to process what’s happening before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.520
he sees the red dot shining&nbsp;
on the end of Gojo’s finger.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:06.120
Jogo’s body goes flying at insane speeds,&nbsp;
unfortunately causing innocent bystanders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:12.520
to burst into flames on the way. But hey,&nbsp;
so far, Gojo didn’t technically kill anybody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:17.840
himself - we’re still going to count those deaths&nbsp;
as being caused by Jogo’s flying, fiery body.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:24.120
The volcano curse smacks right into the&nbsp;
barrier outside Shibuya Station at top speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.080
instantly destroying him in a&nbsp;
fiery explosion. But someday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:34.480
if enough people fear a volcanic eruption, he’ll&nbsp;
be born again. See you again someday, Jogo.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.840
Up next is Hanami, who would have been very&nbsp;
disturbed by his friend’s death if he could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:46.240
see it - but since he’s got twigs for eyes,&nbsp;
it probably won’t bother him much. Speaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:52.120
of those twigs, by the time he registers that&nbsp;
Jogo is gone, Gojo has grabbed his eye branches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:58.440
and ripped them straight out of his head. You see,&nbsp;
the mangaka Gege Akutami already wrote Hanami the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:04.600
perfect death - so he’ll get destroyed immediately&nbsp;
after this by being crushed by Gojo’s infinite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:11.920
technique. Hanami loves nature, so it’s fitting&nbsp;
that he’d be destroyed by a freak of nature.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:17.280
Currently Dagon, the ocean disaster curse&nbsp;
is shyly hiding behind a post in the Subway&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:25.480
Station. Not for long. Dagon holds power over&nbsp;
water. The peaceful, blue sea: and it just so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:32.880
happens that Gojo also has something blue -&nbsp;
his Cursed Technique: Lapse Blue. Dagon isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.240
going to be hiding for long because he’ll&nbsp;
be pulled toward Gojo with immense force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:43.080
breaking straight through the pillar. He might get&nbsp;
a few innocent bystanders soaked along the way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:49.560
but by the time he gets to Gojo, it’s not long&nbsp;
before this poor curse is turned into sushi.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.880
In the actual story, we eventually&nbsp;
get to see the full range of Dagon’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:58.280
powers. There’s a reason he’s a Special&nbsp;
Grade Curse along with his teammates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.360
but all you anime viewers will just&nbsp;
have to keep watching to find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:06.360
what he can do because in our What&nbsp;
If scenario…this guy is super dead.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:12.080
The Disaster Curses have one more ally available&nbsp;
to bide time for the rest of the reinforcements to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:18.880
arrive: Choso, the Cursed Womb: Death Painting.&nbsp;
This powerful combination of a human and cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:24.160
spirit wants to avenge his brothers, the other&nbsp;
Death Paintings. Using his power of blood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:36.360
manipulation, he fires a shot of blood at Gojo.&nbsp;
However, as we know, Gojo is untouchable. Using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:42.200
his infinity powers, the blood appears to stop&nbsp;
just short of striking him. However, in reality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:47.800
the blood is approaching him, just so slowly that&nbsp;
it will never actually reach him because it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:54.760
traveling through the technically infinite amount&nbsp;
of space between any two objects. Math is hard.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.320
Being not at all hit by Choso’s attack&nbsp;
means that Gojo can easily approach the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:06.200
Death Painting and eliminate him with&nbsp;
deadly force. Choso sadly won’t get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:11.880
to avenge his brother, but on the bright&nbsp;
side he does get to see them real soon.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:18.200
It’s at this point that a subway car&nbsp;
rolls into the station. Out bursts Mahito,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:24.000
laughing maniacally as he reveals his train&nbsp;
full of transfigured humans. “Surely Gojo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:28.960
didn’t count on this!” he thinks, before&nbsp;
looking around. His eyes go wide as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:34.360
sees Gojo’s beautiful blue eyes staring&nbsp;
back at him. He is strangely not occupied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:41.760
at all by fighting the other disaster curses.&nbsp;
Instead, all of Mahito’s friends are super dead.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:46.800
Uh oh, how will Gojo deal with all&nbsp;
of these transfigured humans? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.960
similar to the way he does in the regular&nbsp;
series. By activating his domain expansion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:56.760
unlimited void. This extension of Gojo’s&nbsp;
limitless ability brings infinity right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:02.680
into the minds of everyone exposed to it. It&nbsp;
unleashes an infinite amount of raw information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:07.400
right into the brains of its victims,&nbsp;
completely immobilizing them. They feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:14.880
and see and hear everything all at the same&nbsp;
time and are overwhelmed, left to slowly die.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.080
Gojo’s special trick during the&nbsp;
Shibuya Incident was to spare the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:24.320
civilians this fate by only activating&nbsp;
his domain expansion for .2 seconds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:28.240
leaving them unconscious, but not&nbsp;
killing them. However, this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:34.200
his Geto senses are tingling as his old friend&nbsp;
and enemy shows up with the Prison Realm.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:41.360
In an instant, he knows two things. One:&nbsp;
This is not Geto - I totally killed him. Two:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:44.880
If I let whoever this impostor&nbsp;
is do whatever they’re planning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:50.040
things are going to end up really&nbsp;
bad. You can’t make an omelet without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:55.560
breaking a few eggs, and in this case&nbsp;
Gojo’s eggs are innocent civilians.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:09:00.080
However, along with all of the regular&nbsp;
humans - this also takes out Mahito’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:06.760
legion of transfigured humans.&nbsp;
At this point Gojo would be BIG&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:11.800
MAD. Not only has his bestie’s corpse&nbsp;
been taken over by some evil force,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:17.120
but this team of baddies has gotten him&nbsp;
to break his one rule and kill a bunch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:22.760
of innocent people. Not only does he kill them&nbsp;
by using his domain, but he essentially forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:28.880
them to suffer for what feels like eternity.&nbsp;
He’s not about to let them get away with that.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:34.880
Mahito can transfigure someone into a monstrous&nbsp;
new form just by touching them. He does so by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.280
changing the shape of their soul, and the&nbsp;
body follows this new twisted shape. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.280 --> 00:10:00.680
as established, it’s pretty much impossible&nbsp;
to touch Gojo. His domain wouldn’t have enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:06.600
power to overcome Gojo’s Unlimited Void.&nbsp;
Failing to touch and transform Satoru Gojo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:12.160
Mahito would try to run away, but he’d&nbsp;
be unable to make any progress - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:17.240
space in front of him would infinitely&nbsp;
extend making it impossible for him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:22.000
get away from Gojo before he was hit&nbsp;
by the full effect of Unlimited Void.

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:28.400
Pseudo Geto is another story, though.&nbsp;
This sorcerer has been around the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:34.080
block and knows more than anyone about&nbsp;
Gojo’s abilities. Using a simple domain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:40.000
he nullifies the effects of Unlimited Void and&nbsp;
brings the two back to a more even playing ground.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:44.120
Pseudo Geto would use his signature&nbsp;
ability to fight against Gojo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:48.560
which is summoning the cursed spirits that he’s&nbsp;
captured with his cursed technique. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:53.280
just like everyone else - the spirits&nbsp;
would have a very hard time even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.280 --> 00:11:02.080
hitting Gojo. And at this point we’re&nbsp;
dealing with an extremely angry Gojo.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:06.680
He has one technique left that he’s been&nbsp;
saving up and Geto is the perfect sorcerer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:12.720
to use it on. Combining his red and blue&nbsp;
powers, he uses his Hollow Purple technique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:18.520
the same power he developed in order to&nbsp;
defeat Toji Fushiguro. This immense blast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:23.120
of energy would absolutely destroy&nbsp;
Pseudo-Geto before he even gets to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:27.720
tauntingly reveal his evil brain or&nbsp;
his hidden identity. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:33.720
Hollow Purple would also absolutely destroy&nbsp;
Shibuya Station and most of the people in it.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:40.640
Ultimately, it’s worth it based on how&nbsp;
many additional citizens of Japan this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:49.320
move would actually save. And, while also&nbsp;
remaining somewhat vague…there are probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:54.160
still going to be some innocent people who&nbsp;
die in Shibuya whether Gojo kills them or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.160 --> 00:12:00.400
not. The only difference is whether he gets&nbsp;
sealed and even more people die eventually.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.600
After this sweeping move, the show would&nbsp;
pretty much be over. With the disaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:09.560
curses and Pseudo Geto out of the way, the&nbsp;
biggest threats to humanity are gone and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:13.760
Jujutsu High can carry on business&nbsp;
as usual, saving Japan from curses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:18.280
that are not special grade. You know,&nbsp;
just regular run-of-the-mill curses.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:22.760
The remainder of the show could focus on&nbsp;
Yuji going on a quest for the remainder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:28.400
of Sukuna’s fingers and devouring them all like a&nbsp;
delicious gourmet meal until he’s finally executed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:35.240
by the worst school administration of all time.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Gojo would suffer from crippling PTSD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:40.560
after having killed a bunch of innocent people&nbsp;
by his own hand (or his own cursed technique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:46.440
I should say). Therapy is a much smaller price to&nbsp;
pay than Japan being overrun by curses, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:52.280
so hopefully he can learn to forgive himself and&nbsp;
return to the same old Gojo we know and love.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.800
Speaking of that Gojo we know and&nbsp;
love - obviously he’s one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.840
coolest characters in all of anime, but if&nbsp;
you want to learn exactly what makes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:05.800
such an amazingly written character - you can&nbsp;
check out this character analysis video next!

